    "title": "Traffic update: Beaumont highways backed up for evening drive - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Bianca Thomas ,\n1 days ago This photo shows a picture of I-10 taken on August 8, 2025. (Bianca Thomas/The Enterprise) Another day of rainy weather is bringing backed up traffic on Beaumont highways.\nInterstate 10 west is congested this evening, according to the TxDOT traffic maps and cameras. Drivers coming from Vidor and Rose City may encounter slow traffic that begins near the Neches River at Marina Street and continues past the I-10 and U.S. 90 interchange near Pine Street. The congestion continues down I-10 past Babe Zaharias Park and ends before U.S. 69 near 13th Street.\nDrivers on U.S. 69 can also expect traffic in both directions. Southbound traffic is congested between Austin Street and North Street, according to the TxDOT map.\nNorthbound traffic on U.S. 69 slows near Fannet Road and Ward Drive. According to TxDOT traffic map, congestion continues down U.S. 69 and ends at the I-10 interchange near Corporate Drive and Washington Boulevard.\nSign up for Beaumont Enterprise newsletters here\nRead the original article on beaumontenterprise.com\n4",
